      "candidate": "```python\n# repaired_scraper.py\n# This script uses Scrapy\u2019s Item objects but guarantees that the returned\n# mapping is a plain Python `dict`, not a `mappingproxy`.\n\nimport scrapy\nfrom scrapy import Item, Field\n\nclass GPUItem(Item):\n    product_id   = Field()\n    title        = Field()\n    price        = Field()\n    availability = Field()\n    rating       = Field()\n    url          = Field()\n\nclass GPUPriceSpider(scrapy.Spider):\n    name = \"gpu_price\"\n    start_urls = [\"https://example.test/gpu-1\"]\n\n    def parse(self, response):\n        item = GPUItem()\n        item['product_id'] = response.css('.product-id::text').get()\n        item['title'] = response.css('h1.title::text').get()\n        price_text = response.css('.price::text').re_first(r'\\$([0-9,]+\\.?[0-9]?)')\n        if price_text:\n            item['price'] = int(price_text.replace(',', ''))\n        availability_text = response.css('.availability::text').re_first(r'(\\w+)')\n        if availability_text:\n            item['availability'] = (\n                'in_stock' if availability_text.lower() == 'in stock'\n                else 'out_of_stock'\n            )\n        rating_text = response.css('.rating::attr(data-rating)').get()\n        if rating_text:\n            item['rating'] = float(rating_text)\n        item['url'] = response.url\n\n        # Convert to a plain dict before returning.\n        yield dict(item)\n```\n\n**What changed**\n\nThe original scraper returned `scrapy.Item` objects which were automatically converted to a `mappingproxy` in the output.  \nThe repaired version explicitly `yield dict(item)` so the result is a regular Python `dict`, matching the `gpu-price-schema-v1` expectation."
